## 0.2 The CMS detector

The central feature of the CMS apparatus is a superconducting solenoid of 6m internal diameter, providing a magnetic field of 3.8T. Within the solenoid volume, the solenoid is a silicon pixel and strip tracker, the crystal electromagnetic calorimeter, and the brass and scintillator detectors. The crystal electromagnetic calorimeter is composed of brass and scintillator plates, covering the pseudorapidity range \(\abs{\eta}<2.5\). The crystal electromagnetic calorimeter is composed of brass and scintillator plates, covering the pseudorapidity range \(\abs{\eta}<2.

